        let ben2: [String: String] = ["team.regeln.intro": "How teams work on pumpfoil.org: who sees what, how things are scored, and what happens when something is deleted.", "team.regeln.was.titel": "What is a team?", "team.regeln.was.text": "A fixed group with its own leaderboards, events and team chat.\nAnyone can start teams, several if they like, and be in several teams.\nA new team works right away, through invite links.", "team.regeln.rollen.titel": "Roles", "team.regeln.rollen.text": "The team lead can do everything: settings, leaderboards, events, naming moderators, handing over the lead and deleting the team.\nModerators accept or decline requests, remove members and create events. They can't change anything else.\nMembers see everything in the team and can leave at any time.\nThe lead can only leave after handing over the lead.", "team.regeln.beitreten.titel": "Joining", "team.regeln.beitreten.text": "If a team allows sign-ups, its page shows a “Join” button. Depending on the setting you're in right away, or the lead or a moderator decides.\nThere are two invite links: one that makes you a member right away and one that sends a request. Both are also available as QR codes.\nAnyone without an account creates one and is then straight in the team, or has sent the request.\nA newly created link replaces the old one, which then stops working.\nEvery time you join, you agree that the team's leaderboards may be public, even if they aren't right now.\nWith a request, the team lead and moderators see which spots and sports you have been out on so far (only the number of sessions).", "team.regeln.oeffentlich.titel": "What is public", "team.regeln.oeffentlich.text": "Inside, a team can do anything. It only appears to others once we've looked at and approved its name, address, description, crest and colour.\nThe team banner goes through the same approval as the crest. The team lead chooses which part is visible without a new approval; if they remove the banner, it disappears from the public page right away too.\nIf an approved team changes its appearance, that applies inside the team right away, and to the public after a new approval.\nApproved teams are listed on the “All teams” page, and their current and upcoming events in the community.\nIf the lead makes the leaderboards public, everyone can see them, even without signing in, but only rank, display name, initials and value. Sessions, spots, dates and profile pictures are visible to signed-in users only.\nSearch engines don't index team pages.\nThe lead decides who sees the member list: members only, or all signed-in users.", "team.regeln.bestenlisten.titel": "Leaderboards", "team.regeln.bestenlisten.text": "Each person counts once: their best value from a single session, or for totals everything in the chosen period added up.\nAll of a member's sessions count, including those from before they joined. Anyone who leaves disappears from the lists right away.\nFor events this only applies until the end, see “Events”.\nThe same filters apply as for the community records: deleted, reported, unassigned and ongoing recordings don't count.\nEach leaderboard can be limited to one sport, a foil band, recordings with motion data, the phone on the board, or the team spots.\nIf “Hide location” is on, the session never counts for a particular spot.\nOn a tie, whoever rode the value first comes first.", "team.regeln.statistik.titel": "Team totals", "team.regeln.statistik.text": "Above the leaderboards are the totals of all members in the chosen period: pumps, on-foil distance and time, sessions, runs and how many members were active.\nThere's deliberately no team-versus-team ranking.", "team.regeln.logbuch.titel": "Logbook", "team.regeln.logbuch.text": "The logbook records who broke which team record, and when. It's updated every night.\nThe first entry of a leaderboard is the standing on the first night after it was set up.\nFor best values every improvement counts, including your own. For totals it only counts when someone takes the lead.\nIf a record drops because a session was deleted or someone left, it's adjusted quietly, without an entry.", "team.regeln.chat.titel": "Team chat", "team.regeln.chat.text": "Only active members can read and write in the team chat. Anyone who has only sent a request can't see it.\nIt never shows up for others, not even among the active chats.\nAnyone who leaves or is removed loses access right away and gets no more notifications.", "team.regeln.loeschen.titel": "Deleting a team", "team.regeln.loeschen.text": "Only the team lead can delete a team, and only by typing the team name to confirm.\nThe team is then gone for everyone: memberships, leaderboards, logbook, events and the team chat. We keep the data for now so a team deleted by mistake can be restored.\nThe team's address stays blocked and is never given to another team.", "team.regeln.konto.titel": "When an account is deleted", "team.regeln.konto.text": "The person disappears from all teams and leaderboards, and from frozen event results too. Those below move up.\nIf they led a team, the longest-serving moderator takes over, otherwise the longest-serving member. If nobody is left, the team is deleted.", "team.regeln.haftung.titel": "Liability", "team.regeln.haftung.text": "Events are run by the teams themselves. pumpfoil.org has no influence on events or on any promises made in them, financial or otherwise, and accepts no responsibility for them. Recourse to the courts is excluded. Payments and all other arrangements are settled between organisers and participants, independently of pumpfoil.org.\nLikewise, pumpfoil.org accepts no responsibility for whether measured values and data are correct or have been manipulated. What is shown is what the public source code on GitHub calculates from the uploaded data; there are no further promises.", "team.regeln.events.titel": "Events", "notif.typeComment": "Comments on my sessions", "home.topCommented": "Most commented", "theme.dark": "Dark", "theme.light": "Light", "tech.hLong": "Runs from 20 s – steady middle", "tech.hShort": "Runs under 20 s – whole run", "tech.lShort": "Runs between 5 and 20 s, each including start and end.", "tech.allRuns": "All runs", "account.tabGuide": "Guide", "tab.watchSettings": "Settings", "account.tabConnect": "My watch(es)", "account.tabFaces": "Watch faces / Data fields", "account.tabAlarm": "On-Foil Alarm", "account.tabCompat": "Compatibility", "account.toLayouts": "Custom layouts", "tab.watchSettingsUhr": "Watch settings", "guide.appleSub": "watchOS 9+", "guide.a.s1Title": "1. Install the app:", "guide.a.s1": "from the App Store.", "guide.a.s2Title": "2. Connect — optional:", "guide.a.s2a": "You can record immediately without an account (“Connect later”) and upload the session afterwards. To link it: in the watch app “Connect” → “Generate pairing code” — enter the shown code here in the tab"]
        men.merge(ben2) { a, _ in a }
        let ben3: [String: String] = ["guide.a.s2b": ".", "guide.a.s3Title": "3. Data fields:", "guide.a.s3": "swipeable pages right on the watch (configurable in the “Data fields” tab). Stop button at the start and end of the pages.", "guide.a.s4Title": "4. Record:", "guide.a.s4": "open the app → Start → foil → Stop. Recording also works offline; sync happens automatically once online.", "guide.wearSub": "Samsung Galaxy Watch, Google Pixel Watch …", "guide.w.s1Title": "1. Install the app on the watch:", "guide.w.s1": "open the Play Store on the watch and search for “Pumpfoil”.", "guide.w.s1Note": "The Play Store on your phone installs the phone app — the watch app is a separate install, on the watch itself.", "guide.w.s2Title": "2. Connect — optional:", "guide.w.s2a": "like Apple Watch — recording without an account is possible, connect later; or in the watch app “Connect” → “Generate pairing code” and enter the code here in the tab", "guide.w.s2b": ".", "guide.w.s3Title": "3. Data fields:", "guide.w.s3": "swipeable pages, configurable in the “Data fields” tab.", "guide.w.s4Title": "4. Record:", "guide.w.s4": "open the app → Start → foil → Stop. Offline recording + automatic sync.", "guide.amazfitSub": "Our recorder runs on Amazfit watches with Zepp OS (Balance, T-Rex 3, Cheetah, Active 2/3 and more).", "guide.z.store": "Get the Zepp app, then find Pumpfoil in its built-in App Store:", "guide.z.s1": "Install the Zepp app (above) and pair your Amazfit in it as usual.", "guide.z.s2": "In the Zepp app: Profile → your Amazfit → App Store → search “Pumpfoil” → Install.", "guide.z.s3": "Open Pumpfoil on the watch, swipe to ›Connect‹ for a code, then enter it under ", "guide.z.s4": "Press START to record. GPS and heart rate upload automatically over Wi-Fi or your phone.", "guide.huaweiSub": "Our recorder runs on the HUAWEI WATCH 5 (HarmonyOS 5/6). Once linked, the watch uploads on its own – no phone app needed.", "guide.h.s1": "On the watch, open AppGallery, search for “Pumpfoil” and install it. Allow location and body sensors.", "guide.h.s2": "Open Pumpfoil, swipe up to the settings and tap ›pumpfoil.org‹ – the watch shows a code. Enter it under ", "guide.h.s3": "Tap START. Hold STOP and Pause for 2 seconds, tap Discard twice.", "guide.h.s4": "After stopping, the watch uploads on its own as soon as it has internet (Wi-Fi or via the paired phone). The start screen then shows “All sent”.", "guide.preview": "What it looks like on the watch:", "guide.previewVer": "What it looks like on the watch (v1.0.24):", "guide.cap.gStart": "Start: GPS ready → START", "guide.cap.gSettings": "Hold MENU → Settings", "guide.cap.gPairCode": "Connect — code on the watch", "guide.cap.gPairOk": "Connected", "guide.cap.gAlarm1": "Choose alarm", "guide.cap.gAlarm2": "Alarm — foil / fixed values", "guide.cap.gAlarm3": "Alarm — trigger", "guide.cap.onFoil": "While riding", "guide.cap.wConnect": "Connect — code on the watch", "guide.cap.wStart": "Start", "guide.cap.wAlarm": "Choose alarm / foil", "guide.cap.wStats": "Overview: time / distance / HR", "guide.cap.wRun": "Current run", "guide.cap.wStop": "Hold → stop", "guide.cap.aConnect": "Connect — generate code", "guide.cap.aCode": "Code → on pumpfoil.org"]
        men.merge(ben3) { a, _ in a }
        let ben4: [String: String] = ["guide.cap.aStart": "Start", "guide.cap.aAlarm": "Choose alarm + trigger", "guide.cap.aStop": "Stop", "guide.cap.aUpload": "Upload after stopping", "guide.settings.title": "Settings for your watch", "guide.settings.intro": "Once the watch is connected, you will find two controls for each of them under ", "guide.settings.intro2": ". They act on the watch itself — it picks them up the next time you open the app there, no update needed. If battery life matters to you, these are the levers.", "guide.settings.recordTitle": "Recording mode (all watches):", "guide.settings.record": "25 Hz, 10 Hz or GPS only. 10 Hz saves battery and costs almost nothing — we ran both rates over the same sessions: your pump count lands within half a percent, and which parts count as foiling is 99.9% identical.", "guide.settings.gnssTitle": "Satellite systems (Garmin only):", "guide.settings.gnss": "The default is the best your watch can manage — every system across two frequency bands. That finds your position fastest and holds onto it best, but it costs real battery. “Without second frequency band” keeps every system and drops only the costly extra band: the most saved for the least lost.", "guide.settings.gpsWarn": "GPS only saves the most, but it throws away pump count, cadence and glide phases altogether — exactly the numbers this app exists for. Pick it only if your watch otherwise will not last the session.", "guide.settings.zepp": "On Amazfit the recording mode has no effect yet — the watch records at its own rate. It does take its language, pause view and custom layouts from here.", "watches.title": "Supported watches", "watches.intro": "Which watch gives which data — you decide. Long-term we want to support all common sports watches.", "watches.colDevice": "Watch", "watches.colGps": "GPS · distance · speed", "watches.colHr": "Heart rate", "watches.colPump": "Pumps & glide phases", "watches.colStatus": "Status", "watches.foot": "Pumps & glide phases need raw acceleration (≥25 Hz) straight from the watch. GPS stats can be analyzed via FIT/data import for many brands.", "watches.legYes": "fully supported", "watches.legPartial": "limited", "watches.legNo": "not available", "watches.linkAccount": "Account linking available", "watches.linkViaSuunto": "via Mi Fitness → Suunto", "watches.nGarmin": "Older models without raw accel: GPS stats are still analyzed.", "watches.nApple": "Raw acceleration via Core Motion.", "watches.nWear": "Runs on any Wear OS 3+ watch — Samsung Galaxy Watch, Google Pixel Watch, TicWatch/Mobvoi, Fossil, OnePlus.", "watches.nAmazfit": "Sensor access depends on the model.", "watches.nHuaweiW5": "Uploads on its own after linking with a code, no phone app needed. New on AppGallery.", "watches.nHuawei": "In progress: records on the watch, transfers via the Pumpfoil app on an Android phone. Which data the watches deliver still needs testing.", "watches.nPolar": "Link your account → import workouts (GPS + HR). The API export doesn't include the high-rate raw accel stream needed for pump detection (only via a separate BLE sensor).", "watches.nSuunto": "Link your account → import workouts (GPS + HR). The FIT export doesn't (yet) include the high-rate raw accel stream needed for pump detection.", "watches.nXiaomi": "No app on the watch (Xiaomi allows no third-party apps). But Mi Fitness officially pushes your workouts into the Suunto app — link Suunto and they arrive here. Instructions under “Linked accounts”.", "watches.nFitbit": "Third-party apps were discontinued.", "watches.nStrava": "An import would be technically possible, but the API does not provide high-rate raw accelerometer data (so no pump detection), and it sits behind a paywall plus API terms that do not fit an open project — deliberately not integrated.", "watches.subStrava": "activity portal", "watches.st.avail": "Available", "watches.st.planned": "awaiting approval", "watches.st.import": "Polar API", "watches.st.no": "Not possible", "watches.st.nope": "nope", "account.recordModeMoved": "Recording rate is now set per watch, with your linked watches."]
        men.merge(ben4) { a, _ in a }
